# ============================================================================
# EmailJS (optional) — contact form email delivery
# ============================================================================
# The contact form works out of the box with a client-side SIMULATED submit
# (no backend required). To enable REAL email delivery via EmailJS, copy this
# file to a local, git-ignored env file and fill in real values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the client bundle by Vite
# (read as import.meta.env.VITE_*). When these are unset/empty, the contact
# form (src/hooks/useContactForm.js) transparently falls back to its simulated
# submit, so the app never breaks.
#
# Where to find these values (EmailJS dashboard — https://www.emailjs.com/):
#   VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID   -> Email Services
#   VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID  -> Email Templates
#   VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY   -> Account > API Keys (publishable public key)
#
# SECURITY: put REAL values only in .env.local (ignored via the *.local rule
# in .gitignore) — never commit them. The public key is browser-publishable;
# do NOT place any private/secret keys in the client env.
# Post-merge prerequisite for real delivery:  npm install @emailjs/browser
# ============================================================================

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
